        "Could not read the page. The browser did not answer UI Automation, or the page is still loading.",
        "UI Automation is not available or is responding slowly. Please try again in a moment.",
        "Help · Shortcuts",
        "## Typing\n• Press a registered shortcut and the saved content is typed into the field where the cursor is.\n@keys:Ctrl|Alt|1\n• If you don't remember the shortcut, press [Type] on the right of the item. 1Key steps aside and a small window appears. Click the field, then press [Type] in the small window.\n@btns:Type\n> Instead of the small window's [Type], you can press the send-input key (Ctrl+Alt+Enter by default). You can change it in Settings.\n## Quick launch\n• Click a program (first row), folder (second row) or website (third row) in the icon row at the top to open it. With a shortcut set, it opens even while 1Key is locked.\n• Add them with [+ Add] › Program / Folder / Website. The pencil button on the corner of the icon row switches to edit mode: click an icon to change or delete it, drag to reorder.\n• A website opens its http:// or https:// address in the chosen browser (Default, Edge or Chrome). It does not look for an open window; it opens each time you press it.\n> [Change] sets a PNG or ICO image as the icon; [Default] returns to the original icon.\n## Managing items\n• [+ Add] › Frequently used text (one field), Site / app login (ID and PW) or Text for several fields creates an item; click an item to change or delete it. Up to 99 items; a search box appears when there are more than 8.\n## Closing and locking\n• Closing the window (×) keeps 1Key running in the tray. To quit, press the power button at the top right.\n• The lock button locks right away. × on the lock screen asks whether to quit.",
        "Fonts",
        "Pretendard (Copyright (c) 2021, Kil Hyung-jin, SIL Open Font License 1.1). See [View license] for the full text.",
        "View license",
        "Font license · Pretendard",
        "About 1Key",
        "Help · Edit shortcut",
        "## Steps\n• ① Enter a name and content.\n• ② Click the shortcut box and press the keys you want.\n• ③ Press [Save]. Before that, [Test] lets you try it in Notepad.\n@btns:Test|*Save\n## Shortcut\n• Include one of Ctrl, Alt, Shift or Win. PrintScreen · ScrollLock · Pause · F13–F24 also work alone. Backspace clears it.\n@keys:Ctrl|Shift|1\n## Use\n@seg:*Cursor|Linked site/app\n• Cursor: types into the field where the cursor is, in any window. No link needed; with several inputs, Tab moves to the next field.\n• Linked site/app: press [Link] next to an input, click the ID field on that page (or program), then press [Link] in the small window. The ID and password fields are found together. If that page or program is not open, nothing is typed.\n• For programs only input 1 is linked; the other inputs follow with Tab from that field.\n> 1Key reads only the address and the fields' names and positions, never what is written in them.\n## Forms\n• The fields depend on the form chosen in [+ Add]: Frequently used text = one field, Site / app login = ID and PW (the ID is shown, the PW is hidden; the eye button shows it), Text for several fields = several fields.\n• In Text for several fields, the + at the end of the content row adds inputs (up to 4); remove an added input with × next to it.\n## Send Enter\n@seg:Off|*Send|Send except browsers\n• Send: presses Enter after typing (like clicking the login button), in browsers too.\n• Send except browsers: browsers get the text only; other programs also get Enter.\n## Method\n• \"Auto (recommended)\" is usually enough. If a window doesn't take the input, pick another method and check with [Test].\n• To type into windows running as administrator (such as in-house banking), turn on \"Always run as administrator\" in Settings.\n## Switches only for linked site/app items\n• Link each input separately (with 2 inputs): when the ID/password pair isn't found in one go, link each input with its own [Link].\n• Click the field if the cursor does not go in: clicks the linked field on screen when the cursor does not get into it. Off for new items.\n## Cautions\n! Fields inside a browser can't be told apart, so if the cursor moves to another field while typing, 1Key won't notice. The content in that field may then be sent with Enter.\n• Browsers are detected by window type, so some desktop apps built the same way count as browsers too.\n• The clipboard method puts your clipboard back after typing. If another program changed the clipboard meanwhile it isn't restored, and non-text content such as pictures or files can't be restored.",
        "Help · Settings",
        "## Saving\n• Changes apply only when you press [Save]. [Cancel] keeps everything as it was. Pressing [< Back] at the top left with changes asks whether to discard them.\n@btns:Cancel|*Save\n## Startup\n• Start with Windows: turn it on or off and press [Save]; 1Key registers or removes startup. With \"Always run as administrator\" on, it asks once for approval (UAC) and 1Key starts as administrator at sign-in.\n• Tray on start: after you start 1Key and unlock it, it goes to the tray instead of showing the window.\n• Tray widget mode: send the window to the tray while unlocked (× or the widget button above the list) and a cat sits on the right end of the taskbar and watches your mouse pointer; click it to open 1Key. It hides while a full-screen program or the Start menu is in use. It can cover a mascot-sized spot at the bottom of a maximized window.\n• Always run as administrator: turn on to type into programs running as administrator (such as in-house banking). Windows asks for permission each time 1Key starts.\n## Display\n@seg:*System|Light|Dark\n• Theme and language preview right away. Leaving without [Save] restores them. \"System\" follows Windows' light/dark mode and display language.\n• Show program names · Show folder names: whether names appear under the quick-launch icons.\n## Auto-lock\n• Locks when the keyboard and mouse aren't used for that time. With \"Off\", lock it yourself with the lock button above the list when you step away.\n• On lock, open confirmations and help windows close and unfinished actions are cancelled.\n## Master password · Backup file\n@btns:Change|Back up|Restore\n• [Change]: changes the master password.\n• [Back up]·[Restore]: makes a backup file for another PC or a Windows reinstall, or restores from one. See [Help] on that screen for details.\n## Send-input key\n@keys:Ctrl|Alt|Enter\n• Pressing [Type] in the list opens a small window. Click the field, then press this key to type there (same as the small window's [Type]). It works only while the small window is open, and is cancelled after 60 seconds or on lock.\n## Tools\n• Restart as administrator [Restart]: reopens 1Key as administrator, this time only.\n• Advanced settings [Open]: opens the screen with typing speed and diagnostics.",
        "Help · Advanced settings",
        "## Typing speed\n• If typing falls behind or letters are dropped, increase the key interval and the wait before typing. Defaults: interval 20, wait 80.\n## Diagnostics\n• Find out why typing fails: after OK, click the target window within 3 seconds to see why it doesn't take the input and what to do. Capture the result when you ask for help.\n• Check browser fields: after OK, click a browser window within 3 seconds to see the address and the list of fields a site link can read on that page (values are not read).\n• Recent fill results: shows recent results of linked site/app items.\n• [Copy] and [Save to file] in the result boxes send the text as it is (with the title, the 1Key version and the time). Messages with 'Details', such as a failed save, have the same buttons.\n## Resource use\n• Shows the CPU and memory 1Key is using, updated every second. CPU is the share of all cores (as in Task Manager); memory is the working set. Both rise a little while the widget-mode mascot moves.",
        "Help · Change master password",
        "## How to change\n• Enter your current master in \"Enter master password\", and the new one in \"Enter new master password / Confirm\". Whether the two match shows right below.\n• At least 4 characters; 8 or more recommended.\n! If you forget the master password, the saved content can't be recovered.\n## After the change\n• All saved content is encrypted again with the new master.\n• Old settings copies (.bak), if any, still open with the old master. You'll be asked whether to delete them.",
        "The launch list file is too large and was not read. The file is left as it is and program/folder launching is off.",
        "The launch list file could not be read. The file is left as it is and program/folder launching is off.",
        "The launch list file has a format this version does not know (it may come from a newer version). The file is left as it is and not used.",
