        "Help · Backup and restore",
        "## Making a backup file\n• Settings › Backup file [Back up]. Enter your current master in \"Enter master password\", and set a password just for the backup file in \"Enter backup password / Confirm\".\n• Passwords, links, settings and the program list all go in, so you can restore on another PC or after reinstalling Windows.\n! The backup file is locked only by the backup password. Choose a long one you don't use elsewhere, and keep the file somewhere you control (such as a USB drive), not in mail, chat or shared folders. If you forget it, the file can't be restored.\n## Restoring — the PC you use\n• Settings › Backup file [Restore]. You're first asked whether to keep the current settings as a backup file too.\n• Enter only the backup file and the backup password. Your current master password stays.\n## Restoring — new PC or reinstalled Windows\n• On the first setup screen: tray icon menu › Restore from a backup.\n• Enter the backup password and a new master password for this PC (it may be the same as before).\n## After restoring\n• 1Key locks and reads the settings again. Unlock with the master.\n> Programs and folders are checked again on this PC; missing programs are not started.",
        "## Meet the cat\n• Close the 1Key window to the tray and a cat appears on the taskbar (Settings › Tray widget mode).\n• Hover over it to see its name and hearts; right-click it for the play menu.\n> Name the white and the black cat in Settings. [Notebook] in the menu shows how your cat is doing.\n## Growing up\n@stages:6\n• Bean Cake → Mochi → Bread Roll → Loaf → Big Loaf → Mega Loaf. One step every 20 points.\n## Earning points\n@missions:stamp=0|pet=0|treat=0|play=0|toy=0|break=0|pw=0/3|backup=0|master=0\n• Pet · Treat · Play: from the right-click menu. Each counts once every 3 minutes.\n• Paw stamp: your first unlock of the day. Weekends don't break the streak; with auto-lock on, +5 more.\n• Surprise toys: now and then a butterfly, a ball of yarn or a soap bubble pops up. Click it and the cat leaps in to play.\n• Breaks: after 50 minutes of work without a break the cat suggests one. Come back after 5 minutes or more for points.\n• Security habits: change a saved password (three a day) · make a backup (once a week) · change the master password (once in 30 days).\n## Good to know\n> No penalties. While 1Key runs, 1 point fades every 10 minutes, but the cat never gets smaller than Bean Cake.\n• Time while 1Key is closed or the PC sleeps does not count.\n• The black cat (dark theme) will grow by the same rules once its play art is ready.",
